--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
found no match for symbol
dropped the body
--
N5008 [dcl.spec.auto.general]/11-13: a call to a function with a deduced
return type needs the type deduced from the definition at the point of the
call.  A STATIC member function template specialization named directly in a
constructor template's mem-initializer (`m_pathname(_S_convert(source))',
std::filesystem::path) reached the call with the placeholder still in its
type, and `str(<<type:auto>>)' found no constructor: the constructor's body
was dropped.  The callee's definition is now converted before the call is
completed, as for namespace-scope and non-static member functions.
